\pxsm0.8;{\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;NOTES:\P\P1\fSimSun|b0|i0|c134|p2;.\P\P\fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;2. This single-line diagram (SLD) is provided for visual representation only and is not drawn to scale.\P\P3. Provide appropriate strain relief at all harness,
  3
 LYNX, transition, and equipment connection points.\P\P\psm1;4. String polarity shall be verified before connecting the PV harness or LYNX assembly. Do not reverse positive and\fArial|b0|i0|c134|p34; \fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;negative connections.\P\psm0.
  3
9;\P\psm1;5. Installation shall comply with the applicable NEC requirements,\fArial|b0|i0|c134|p34; \fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;local codes, approved listings, project specifications, and the authority having jurisdiction.\P\psm0.9;\P\psm1;6. All connectors
  3
 shall be fully engaged, locked, and protected from mechanical damage, moisture,\fArial|b0|i0|c134|p34; \fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;contamination, and direct\fArial|b0|i0|c134|p34; \fArial|b0|i0|c0|p34;contact with the ground.\P\psm0.8;\P7. Field connection
  1
s shall be installed using the manufacturer-specified tools and torque requirements.\P\P8. Maintain the minimum cable-bending radius specified by the cable and assembly manufacturer.}
